      "title": "RAIWAY: A Large-Wheeled Bipedal Robot With Contact-Informed Blind Locomotion",
      "takeaway": "RAIWAY addresses rolling locomotion of a large-wheeled bipedal robot over irregular and discontinuous terrain, where wheel–terrain contact is hard to instrument and not captured by terrain geometry alone. The framework distills multi-contact events from simulation into a latent representation, and at deployment the controller infers that representation online from proprioception without contact sensing. Real-world experiments report traversal of steep slopes, gravel beds, studded surfaces, and rocky terrain, plus continuous ascent on tested outdoor staircases with riser heights up to 15 cm; the contact-informed controller also outperforms baselines lacking the mechanism on the authors' platform. Inspect how the simulated contact latent is grounded in proprioception and how the baseline comparison is configured.",
